From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:10:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Start Cartouche's part of a game's process

A game Cartouche starts in LiveProcess, so that Cartouche stays open
behind it, runs CartoucheGuestStart before LiveContainer starts the
game. Cartouche's prepare.sh copies it in from its
launcher/LiveProcessSupport folder to LiveProcess/Cartouche/, which the
LiveProcess target builds with the rest of its synchronized folder.

It writes the game's memory where Cartouche's System page reads it, and
turns the Home button of a controller, which nxnative leaves without a
use, into a way back to Cartouche's console. The built-in SideStore,
which also runs in LiveProcess, starts as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJotFb6T6MeX5eX3epy2
---
 LiveProcess/main.m | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/LiveProcess/main.m b/LiveProcess/main.m
index c376fcd..eeb5eca 100644
--- a/LiveProcess/main.m
+++ b/LiveProcess/main.m
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ static NSDictionary *retrievedAppInfo;
 @end
 
 extern int LiveContainerMain(int argc, char *argv[]);
+// Cartouche's part of a game's process (LiveProcess/Cartouche/CartoucheGuest.m).
+extern void CartoucheGuestStart(NSDictionary *appInfo);
 static char **_envp, **_apple = NULL;
 int LiveProcessMain(int argc, char *argv[]) {
     // Let NSExtensionContext initialize, once it's done it will call CFRunLoopStop
@@ -96,6 +98,11 @@ int LiveProcessMain(int argc, char *argv[]) {
         
     }
 
+    // A game Cartouche starts here: its memory goes to Cartouche's System
+    // page and its controller's Home button shows Cartouche's console.
+    if (![appInfo[@"selected"] isEqualToString:@"builtinSideStore"]) {
+        CartoucheGuestStart(appInfo);
+    }
     
     return LiveContainerMain(argc, argv);
 }
